E["item:blueleaf-tuber"] = {t="item",n="Blueleaf Tuber",z="razorfenkraul",s="Beneath Razorfen Kraul, Blueleaf Tubers grow hidden from the surface. Their rarity draws wealthy gourmands and traders from across the world.",h="Beneath Razorfen Kraul, Blueleaf Tubers grow hidden from the surface.",sec={{t="A Rare Underground Delicacy",b="Blueleaf Tubers grow beneath Razorfen Kraul in the Barrens. Dense roots and quilboar briars hide them from casual foragers. Though the ground is harsh, wealthy gourmands and traders across the world pay an exorbitant price for their distinct flavor.",sp=0},{t="Gopher-Assisted Harvesting",b="In Ratchet, the goblin Mebok Mizzyrix devised a way to find the hidden roots. He trains native snufflenose gophers to scent tubers from fifty paces away. Guided by specialized command sticks, adventurers can unearth them before quilboar patrols catch wind of the intrusion.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Blueleaf Tubers used for?",a="Wealthy clients and exotic traders pay a premium for Blueleaf Tubers, drawn by their distinct taste and scarcity.",al={"tuber use","why get blueleaf tubers","what are tubers for"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can Blueleaf Tubers be found?",a="Blueleaf Tubers grow deep underground in Razorfen Kraul, in the southern Barrens, among its briars and subterranean dens.",al={"where do blueleaf tubers grow","tuber location","where are tubers"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do you need a gopher to dig them up?",a="Blueleaf Tubers hide beneath the topsoil, beyond the sight of humans and goblins. Trained snufflenose gophers scent them from fifty paces away and dig them up on command.",al={"why snufflenose gopher","gopher purpose","why gophers"}},{q="Who buys these tubers?",a="The goblin entrepreneur Mebok Mizzyrix, based in Ratchet, buys Blueleaf Tubers to sell to wealthy buyers and international contacts for a hefty profit.",al={"who wants blueleaf tubers","who buys tubers","mebok tubers"},it="motive"},{q="What is a Blueleaf Tuber?",a="A Blueleaf Tuber is an exceedingly rare edible root buried deep beneath the earth in Razorfen Kraul. Prize-worthy for its culinary value, it is considered a delicacy across the world, though gathering it is treacherous given the quilboar infesting its native grounds.",al={"what is blueleaf tuber","blueleaf tuber lore","what are blueleaf tubers"},it="identity",add="9eab4987"},{q="Where does the Blueleaf Tuber come from?",a="Blueleaf Tubers are natural underground roots native solely to the southern Barrens, growing deep within the tangled root systems of Razorfen Kraul. They are not crafted by anyone, but are harvested directly from the subterranean soil using trained snufflenose gophers to scent them out.",al={"blueleaf tuber origin","where do blueleaf tubers grow","who made blueleaf tubers"},it="origin",add="094c1930"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Blueleaf Tubers are a rare culinary delicacy sought by the wealthiest gourmands, though they grow in the harsh dirt of quilboar dens."},kw={"barrens","blueleaf tuber","mebok mizzyrix","ratchet","razorfen kraul","snufflenose gopher","tuber"},rel={"quest:1221","npc:mebok-mizzyrix","item:crate-with-holes","item:snufflenose-command-stick","item:snufflenose-owner-s-manual","zone:razorfenkraul","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},src={"Blueleaf Tuber","Blueleaf Tubers"}}
E["item:crate-with-holes"] = {t="item",n="Crate With Holes",z="razorfenkraul",s="In Ratchet, Mebok Mizzyrix prepares a crate for a Snufflenose Gopher.",h="In Ratchet, Mebok Mizzyrix prepares a crate for a Snufflenose Gopher.",sec={{t="A Sniffer in a Box",b="Mebok Mizzyrix sends trained Snufflenose Gophers to find Blueleaf Tubers in Razorfen Kraul. The gophers cannot follow an adventurer across the Barrens on foot, so Mebok places each one in a wooden crate with air holes. Inside the quilboar stronghold, the crate is opened and the gopher follows its keen nose toward the buried tubers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is inside the Crate With Holes?",a="A living Snufflenose Gopher trained by Mebok Mizzyrix rides inside. Holes in the crate let it breathe as it travels across the Barrens.",al={"what is in the box","crate contents","what is inside"},it="identity"},{q="Where do I get the Crate With Holes?",a="You can take a crate from the pile beside Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet, the port town on the Barrens' eastern coast.",al={"crate location","where to find crate with holes","mebok crate"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="How does the crate work inside Razorfen Kraul?",a="Open the crate inside Razorfen Kraul to release the Snufflenose Gopher. Direct it with a Snufflenose Command Stick, and it will use its nose to find Blueleaf Tubers buried underground.",al={"how to use crate with holes","using crate","summon gopher"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Why are Blueleaf Tubers so hard to find without the gopher?",a="Blueleaf Tubers grow deep underground among Razorfen Kraul's roots, beyond ordinary sight. Snufflenose Gophers can smell them from fifty paces away.",al={"why need gopher","finding tubers","tuber location"}},{q="Where does the Crate With Holes come from, and who made it?",a="The crate is provided by Mebok Mizzyrix, an enterprising goblin merchant operating out of the port town of Ratchet in the Barrens. To harvest the valuable roots hidden within the quilboar stronghold of Razorfen Kraul, Mebok devised a way to transport trained snufflenose gophers safely into the field, punching holes into standard shipping crates so his prized critters can breathe during transport.",al={"crate with holes origin","who made crate with holes","where did crate with holes come from"},it="origin",add="39b6cc8f"},{q="Why does Mebok Mizzyrix want the Crate With Holes back?",a="Mebok expects the crate returned alongside his command stick and the harvested Blueleaf Tubers because trained snufflenose gophers are an investment he cannot afford to lose. The tubers are an exceptionally rare delicacy across the world, and without his trained gophers and their specialized transport crates, finding them buried deep within Razorfen Kraul is virtually impossible.",al={"why does mebok want crate","why is crate with holes wanted","crate with holes purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="08415caf"}},kw={"blueleaf tubers","crate with holes","mebok mizzyrix","ratchet","razorfen kraul","snufflenose gopher"},rel={"quest:1221","npc:mebok-mizzyrix","item:blueleaf-tuber","item:snufflenose-command-stick","item:snufflenose-owner-s-manual","zone:razorfenkraul","subzone:ratchet","topic:goblin"},src={"Crate With Holes","Blueleaf Tubers"}}
E["item:razorflank-s-medallion"] = {t="item",n="Razorflank's Medallion",z="razorfenkraul",s="Charlga Razorflank's medallion lies deep within Razorfen Kraul, carried by the crone who rules the stronghold. Its return gives the night elf sentinels proof that she has fallen.",h="Charlga Razorflank's medallion lies deep within Razorfen Kraul, carried by the crone who rules the stronghold.",sec={{t="Proof of the Crone's Fall",b="Charlga Razorflank carries the medallion as the leader of the Razorfen quilboar. At Thalanaar, Falfindel Waywarder learns of fallen explorers such as Heralath and the dwarf Lonebrow, then sends Alliance adventurers against the quilboar leader. The medallion confirms Charlga's death to the night elf sentinels guarding Feralas's borders. They can know that the gathered forces within the Kraul have lost their leader.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who carries Razorflank's Medallion?",a="Charlga Razorflank carries the medallion deep within Razorfen Kraul. She is the crone who leads the quilboar there.",al={"who drops razorflanks medallion","razorflank medallion source","charlga medallion"},gp=true},{q="Who wants this medallion brought to them?",a="Falfindel Waywarder at Thalanaar asks for the medallion. He wants proof that Charlga has been slain.",al={"who wants razorflank medallion","turn in razorflanks medallion","falfindel medallion"},gp=true},{q="Why does Falfindel need proof of Charlga's death?",a="Charlga gathered a hostile quilboar force within Razorfen Kraul, threatening the surrounding regions. Heralath and Lonebrow were among the scouts who died. The medallion assures the night elves that the immediate threat is broken and lets their investigations continue.",al={"why kill charlga","purpose of medallion","why need medallion"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is Razorflank's Medallion?",a="Razorflank's Medallion is a personal token carried by Charlga Razorflank, the crone and leader of the quilboar dwelling deep within Razorfen Kraul. More than simple ornamentation, it serves as an unmistakable symbol of her authority over the swarming tribes in the Kraul, making it the definitive trophy of her fall.",al={"what is razorflank medallion","razorflanks medallion lore","charlga razorflank medallion"},it="identity",add="b119a669"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance adventurer, recovering the medallion avenges the fallen scout Heralath and the dwarf explorer Lonebrow. It secures Thalanaar's border route into Feralas.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, slaying Charlga and claiming her medallion lets your people safely study Agamaggan's corrupted sacred resting grounds."},kw={"agamaggan","charlga razorflank","falfindel waywarder","lonebrow","razorfen kraul","razorflank's medallion","thalanaar"},rel={"quest:1101","npc:charlga-razorflank","npc:falfindel-waywarder","zone:razorfenkraul","subzone:thalanaar","topic:agamaggan","topic:razorfen","quest:1100"},src={"Razorflank's Medallion","The Crone of the Kraul"}}
E["item:snufflenose-command-stick"] = {t="item",n="Snufflenose Command Stick",z="razorfenkraul",s="In Ratchet, Mebok Mizzyrix sends trained gophers after blueleaf tubers in Razorfen Kraul.",h="In Ratchet, Mebok Mizzyrix sends trained gophers after blueleaf tubers in Razorfen Kraul.",sec={{t="A Rod for Rodents",b="Mebok Mizzyrix has trained snufflenose gophers to find blueleaf tubers deep in Razorfen Kraul. The roots lie hidden beneath the thorny tunnels, where finding them is nearly impossible without help. Mebok, a merchant in Ratchet, avoids entering the quilboar dens himself. He gives adventurers the Snufflenose Command Stick to direct the gophers. From up to fifty paces away, the stick guides them to sniff out and uncover the roots.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Snufflenose Command Stick used for?",a="The Snufflenose Command Stick directs a trained snufflenose gopher to find hidden blueleaf tubers in Razorfen Kraul. Point it at a gopher, and it follows the scent and digs up the roots.",al={"how to use command stick","what does command stick do","command stick purpose"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Where do you obtain the Snufflenose Command Stick?",a="You obtain the Snufflenose Command Stick in Ratchet, just outside Mebok Mizzyrix's workshop. It comes with a crate holding a trained gopher and an instruction manual.",al={"where to get command stick","command stick location","who gives the command stick"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does Mebok Mizzyrix want blueleaf tubers?",a="Mebok Mizzyrix seeks blueleaf tubers because they are rare delicacies that bring substantial profit from affluent culinary contacts around the world. They grow deep beneath the Barrens in quilboar territory, so he hires adventurers to gather them.",al={"why tubers","blueleaf tuber purpose","why does mebok want tubers"},it="motive"},{q="Do you get to keep the stick after finding the tubers?",a="No. After gathering the requested tubers, you return the Snufflenose Command Stick and transport crate to Mebok in Ratchet with your harvest.",al={"can i keep command stick","returning command stick"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="What is the Snufflenose Command Stick?",a="The Snufflenose Command Stick is the patented handling tool of Snuff Inc., supplied with the goblin entrepreneur Mebok Mizzyrix's trained gophers in Ratchet. It is designed specifically to direct trained snufflenose gophers, giving them the signal to root out buried, elusive delicacies that an ordinary scout would completely overlook.",al={"what is command stick","snufflenose stick","what is snufflenose command stick"},it="identity",add="8cc828c2"},{q="Where does the Snufflenose Command Stick come from, and who made it?",a="The command stick is a patented product of Snuff Inc., whose owner Marwig Rustbolt explains its use in the Snufflenose Owner's Manual. Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet trained his snufflenose gophers to harvest rare delicacies and keeps the command sticks, crates and manuals together so hired hands can control the critters properly.",al={"who made the command stick","command stick origin","where does command stick come from"},it="origin",add="9fdd5faa"},{q="Why does anyone want the Snufflenose Command Stick?",a="Rare blueleaf tubers are impossible to spot unaided beneath the brambles of Razorfen Kraul. The command stick is vital because it compels a trained snufflenose gopher to sniff fifty paces out and excavate the tubers, which can then be returned to Mebok Mizzyrix for a handsome payout.",al={"why do you need the stick","why is the command stick wanted","why get snufflenose command stick"},it="why_wanted",add="fb1cfa60"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Blueleaf tubers are prized as a culinary delicacy around the world. You need a trained animal and a handler's stick to find them, rather than ordinary kitchen tools."},kw={"blueleaf tuber","command stick","gopher","mebok mizzyrix","ratchet","razorfen kraul","snufflenose","the barrens"},rel={"npc:mebok-mizzyrix","quest:1221","item:blueleaf-tuber","item:crate-with-holes","item:snufflenose-owner-s-manual","zone:razorfenkraul","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},src={"Snufflenose Command Stick","Blueleaf Tubers"}}
E["item:snufflenose-owner-s-manual"] = {t="item",n="Snufflenose Owner's Manual",z="razorfenkraul",s="In Ratchet, Mebok Mizzyrix keeps Snufflenose Owner's Manual beside him. Marwig Rustbolt of Snuff Inc. wrote the booklet to explain how to send a trained Snufflenose Gopher after Blueleaf Tubers in Razorfen Kraul.",h="In Ratchet, Mebok Mizzyrix keeps Snufflenose Owner's Manual beside him.",sec={{t="A Goblin's Operating Guide",b="Marwig Rustbolt, owner of Snuff Inc., wrote a guide to handling the company's trained snufflenose gophers. Their keen noses can detect Blueleaf Tubers buried underground from fifty paces away. The manual explains how to release a gopher from a ventilated crate and guide its rooting with a command stick. Prospectors direct it through Razorfen Kraul's thorns and quilboar tunnels to find the tubers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the purpose of the Snufflenose Owner's Manual?",a="The manual explains how to release Mebok Mizzyrix's trained snufflenose gopher from its crate and guide it with a command stick to find Blueleaf Tubers in Razorfen Kraul.",al={"what does the manual do","why read the manual","manual purpose"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can I find the manual?",a="You can find the manual in Ratchet, beside Mebok Mizzyrix and the crates and command sticks used to gather tubers.",al={"manual location","where is the book","how to get the manual"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why are snufflenose gophers needed to find Blueleaf Tubers?",a="Blueleaf Tubers lie buried deep in Razorfen Kraul, where they are nearly impossible for humanoids to spot. A trained gopher can smell one from fifty paces away.",al={"why use gophers","can i find tubers without gophers"},it="motive"},{q="Who wrote the manual?",a="Marwig Rustbolt, owner of Snuff Inc., signed the manual. He wrote it to teach new owners how to feed, walk and command their gophers with the patented command stick.",al={"author of manual","who made it"},it="origin"},{q="What is the Snufflenose Owner's Manual?",a="It is an instructional handbook provided alongside a trained snufflenose gopher and command stick. The manual guides adventurers on how to handle the creature within the subterranean tunnels of Razorfen Kraul, explaining how to command the gopher to sniff out elusive underground Blueleaf Tubers.",al={"what is snufflenose owners manual","snufflenose manual identity","what is the manual"},it="identity",add="1c231f00"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="The manual explains how to retrieve Blueleaf Tubers, an underground root prized as a rare delicacy by gourmands and traders across Azeroth."},kw={"blueleaf tuber","gopher","manual","mebok mizzyrix","ratchet","razorfen kraul","snufflenose"},rel={"quest:1221","npc:mebok-mizzyrix","item:blueleaf-tuber","item:crate-with-holes","item:snufflenose-command-stick","zone:razorfenkraul","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},src={"Snufflenose Owner's Manual","Blueleaf Tubers"}}
E["item:treshala-s-pendant"] = {t="item",n="Treshala's Pendant",z="razorfenkraul",s="In Razorfen Kraul, a pendant carries the bond between Treshala and Heralath Fallowbrook. Heralath brought it from their home in Darnassus into southern Kalimdor, where the quilboar tore it from him as he lay dying.",h="In Razorfen Kraul, a pendant carries the bond between Treshala and Heralath Fallowbrook.",sec={{t="Token of Devotion",b="Heralath Fallowbrook carried the pendant close when he left Teldrassil on perilous journeys. The necklace reminded him of home and of his beloved wife, Treshala, and the devotion they shared.",sp=0},{t="Lost in the Briars",b="Heralath ventured into Razorfen Kraul with his party, where savage quilboar fell upon them. In his final moments, one of the tusked defenders tore the pendant from him. As his life ebbed away, Heralath asked a passing adventurer to wrest the keepsake from his killers and carry it, with news of his fate, home to Treshala in Darnassus.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Treshala's Pendant?",a="Treshala's Pendant belongs to Treshala Fallowbrook. Her husband Heralath carried it as a keepsake of their union before he met his end in Razorfen Kraul.",al={"what is this item","pendant of bonding","who owns the pendant"},it="identity"},{q="How did the pendant end up in Razorfen Kraul?",a="Heralath Fallowbrook carried the pendant on an expedition into Razorfen Kraul. After quilboar ambushed and mortally wounded him, one of them took the necklace from him.",al={"why is it in rfk","how was it lost"}},{q="Who asks for the pendant to be recovered?",a="As he lies dying in Razorfen Kraul, Heralath Fallowbrook begs passing adventurers to recover the pendant and return it to his wife in Darnassus with news of his death.",al={"who gives the quest","who wants the pendant back"}},{q="Who receives the pendant once it is recovered?",a="Treshala Fallowbrook receives the recovered pendant. Heralath's widow lives in Darnassus, the night elf capital atop Teldrassil.",al={"where do i take the pendant","who is treshala"}},{q="Why is Treshala's Pendant wanted?",a="As the dying night elf Heralath Fallowbrook draws his final breaths within Razorfen Kraul, his last wish is for this stolen keepsake to be recovered. It is a pendant of bonding given to him by his wife, Treshala. Before he perishes alone in the quilboar stronghold, he hopes you will retrieve it from the brutes who took it and deliver both the pendant and the somber news of his death to his wife in Darnassus.",al={"why find treshalas pendant","why does herald want the pendant","treshalas pendant purpose"},it="why_wanted",add="1ac8940a"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you can honor a fellow kaldorei who perished far from the safety of Teldrassil's boughs by recovering the pendant.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance member, you can carry the token to Darnassus and bring somber closure to a widow mourning her fallen explorer."},kw={"darnassus","heralath fallowbrook","mortality wanes","quilboar","razorfen kraul","treshala fallowbrook","treshala's pendant"},rel={"quest:1142","npc:treshala-fallowbrook","zone:razorfenkraul","zone:darnassus","topic:quilboar"},src={"Treshala's Pendant","Mortality Wanes"}}
E["npc:agathelos-the-raging"] = {t="npc",n="Agathelos the Raging",z="razorfenkraul",s="Deep within Razorfen Kraul, Agathelos the Raging is penned among the thorned tunnels. His great size matters to the quilboar, who revere Agamaggan as their god and progenitor, and rage makes the armored boar more fearsome still. His strength and mass make him one of the most dangerous beasts beneath the southern Barrens.",h="Deep within Razorfen Kraul, Agathelos the Raging is penned among the thorned tunnels.",sec={{t="Avatars of the Great Boar",b="Agamaggan, a titanic boar, is the god and progenitor of the quilboar. Among the Razorfen tribes, a beast as large as Agathelos carries deep spiritual meaning. He stands roughly twice as tall as a Barrens thunder lizard.",sp=0},{t="Kept in Chains",b="The quilboar keep Agathelos from roaming freely through the Kraul. Several guards maintain a field in front of the short, dead-end tunnel where he is penned. Intruders who break through the barrier face a raging beast, made even bigger and more terrifying by his fury.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Agathelos so huge?",a="Agathelos is a naturally colossal armored boar, roughly twice the size of a common thunder lizard. He grows even bigger when enraged. The quilboar revere Agamaggan, their titanic boar god and progenitor, so a beast of Agathelos's size carries great spiritual meaning.",al={"why is agathelos big","agathelos size","giant boar barrens"},it="power"},{q="Why do the quilboar keep him locked behind a barrier?",a="The quilboar pen Agathelos in a short tunnel behind a field maintained by several guards. The barrier keeps the monstrous, raging boar from roaming the Kraul freely.",al={"agathelos barrier","why is agathelos caged","agathelos force field"},it="why_here"},{q="What is his connection to Agamaggan?",a="Agamaggan is the great boar Ancient and progenitor of the quilboar. His ancestry gives a gigantic boar like Agathelos great spiritual meaning to the quilboar.",al={"agathelos agamaggan","is agathelos a god","agamaggan son"},it="ties"},{q="What tribe created Agathelos?",a="Agathelos is a beast, not a creation. The Death's Head quilboar of Razorfen Kraul keep him in a guarded tunnel deep within the thorns.",al={"who made agathelos","who feeds agathelos","agathelos tribe"},it="origin"},{q="Can hunters tame Agathelos?",a="No. Agathelos is an elite, heavily armored monster, too dangerous for a hunter to bring under control.",al={"tame agathelos","can i tame agathelos","hunter agathelos"},gp=true},{q="Who is Agathelos the Raging?",a="Agathelos the Raging is a colossal armored boar kept deep within Razorfen Kraul. To the quilboar, whose god and progenitor Agamaggan was a titanic boar, he carries considerable spiritual significance; he stands roughly twice the size of a common thunder lizard and grows even more monstrous in battle.",al={"who is agathelos","agathelos identity","what is agathelos the raging"},it="identity",add="a8df9e57"},{q="Whose side is Agathelos the Raging on?",a="Agathelos is a beast, not a schemer. He is kept by the quilboar of Razorfen Kraul, penned in a guarded tunnel, and attacks anyone who breaks into his enclosure.",al={"agathelos faction","who does agathelos serve","whose side is agathelos"},it="side",add="28c36899"},{q="What does Agathelos the Raging want?",a="Agathelos has no grand ambitions or cunning schemes of his own. He is consumed by pure feral rage and seeks only to crush, gore, and trample anything that enters his enclosure.",al={"what does agathelos want","agathelos motives","agathelos goals"},it="wants",add="38ca6f4f"},{q="Why is Agathelos the Raging feared?",a="Agathelos is feared for his sheer, terrifying mass and uncontrollable fury. Armored and naturally massive, his size and ferocity swell even further when enraged, making him capable of crushing entire raiding parties beneath his hooves.",al={"why is agathelos feared","how dangerous is agathelos","agathelos reputation"},it="fame",add="be737a36"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a hunter, you can admire Agathelos's predatory bulk, but his endless rage makes him a beast to slay rather than tame.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you hold Agamaggan in high esteem as one of the great Ancients who fell during the War of the Ancients. Seeing one of his colossal kin penned and raging in the Kraul is grim.",["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren attuned to the earth, you know the legends of Agamaggan. The quilboar's corruption of his kindred beasts marks the rot spreading through the Barrens."},kw={"agamaggan","agathelos","boar","death's head","quilboar","raging","razorfen kraul"},rel={"zone:razorfenkraul","topic:agamaggan","topic:quilboar","topic:razorfen"},src={"Agathelos the Raging"}}
E["npc:aggem-thorncurse"] = {t="npc",n="Aggem Thorncurse",z="razorfenkraul",s="In Razorfen Kraul, Aggem Thorncurse bears the title Death's Head Prophet. He calls a boar spirit to his aid when threatened.",h="In Razorfen Kraul, Aggem Thorncurse bears the title Death's Head Prophet.",sec={{t="The Death's Head Prophet",b="Aggem guards part of Razorfen Kraul, where the Death's Head tribe dwells. His shamanic power lets him summon a boar spirit, reflecting the quilboar's reverence for Agamaggan.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Aggem Thorncurse?",a="Aggem is a quilboar shaman and Death's Head Prophet in Razorfen Kraul.",al={"aggem thorncurse","who is aggem","aggem rf kraul"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Aggem Thorncurse be found?",a="Aggem is found inside Razorfen Kraul in the southern Barrens.",al={"aggem location","where is aggem","where to find aggem thorncurse"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What spirit does Aggem call upon?",a="Aggem summons a boar spirit to fight beside him.",al={"aggem spirit","aggem boar spirit"},it="origin"},{q="How does Aggem fight in combat?",a="Aggem uses shamanic magic and calls a boar spirit to fight beside him.",al={"aggem abilities","how does aggem fight"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Is Aggem Thorncurse affiliated with a specific quilboar tribe?",a="Aggem belongs to the Death's Head tribe.",al={"aggem tribe","what tribe is aggem","razorfen quilboar"},it="side"},{q="Why is Aggem Thorncurse here?",a="Aggem stands among the Death's Head quilboar in Razorfen Kraul, defending his tribe's territory.",al={"why is aggem thorncurse in razorfen kraul","aggem thorncurse location why"},it="why_here",add="0a149290"},{q="Who is Aggem Thorncurse tied to?",a="He belongs to the Death's Head tribe and practices the quilboar's shamanic traditions.",al={"aggem thorncurse connections","who is aggem thorncurse allied with"},it="ties",add="32004356"}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you see Aggem call a boar spirit to aid him, a distinctive expression of quilboar shamanism.",["class:Priest"]="As a priest, you hear Aggem's title of prophet, which reflects the spiritual traditions of the quilboar.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help secure Durotar and Mulgore by putting down persistent defenders like Aggem Thorncurse, while the quilboar menace the Barrens."},kw={"aggem","kraul","quilboar","razorfen","thorncurse"},rel={"zone:razorfenkraul","topic:quilboar","topic:razorfen"},src={"Aggem Thorncurse (Classic)"}}
E["npc:blind-hunter"] = {t="npc",n="Blind Hunter",z="razorfenkraul",s="Deep within Razorfen Kraul, the Blind Hunter roosts in the sunless depths. This elusive albino bat prowls the quilboar redoubt, far from common bats near the cavern entrances.",h="Deep within Razorfen Kraul, the Blind Hunter roosts in the sunless depths.",sec={{t="Depths of the Kraul",b="Razorfen Kraul winds through briars and dark caverns below ground. Common bats roost nearer the surface, where faint light reaches in from outside. The Blind Hunter keeps to the furthest, darkest alcoves of the tangle. Its pale hide and milky gaze may come from generations spent apart from natural sunlight.",sp=0},{t="A Rare Quarry",b="The Blind Hunter is thought to have lost most or all of its ordinary sight. Scholars and scouts believe it tracks prey through the gloom with keen hearing and echolocation. It rarely appears, hunting only now and then among the dense thickets. For cavern explorers, seeing this phantom beast is a rare encounter.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Blind Hunter?",a="The Blind Hunter is a rare albino bat in the deepest, darkest tunnels of Razorfen Kraul. Its pale coloring and elusive habits set it apart from the common bats nearer the entrance.",al={"who is blind hunter","what is blind hunter","blind hunter bat"},it="identity"},{q="Where does the Blind Hunter appear?",a="The Blind Hunter roosts along Razorfen Kraul's shadowed inner paths, past the point where daylight from outside fades away.",al={"blind hunter location","where to find blind hunter","blind hunter spawn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Is the Blind Hunter actually blind?",a="Naturalists and adventurers suspect the Blind Hunter is blind, given its milky eyes and deep-cave home. Its hunting remains sharp, guided by keen hearing and echolocation.",al={"is it blind","can blind hunter see"}},{q="Can hunters tame the Blind Hunter?",a="Yes. Beastmasters who can handle winged predators can tame the Blind Hunter, a distinctive pale companion for those patient enough to find it.",al={"can i tame blind hunter","blind hunter tameable","blind hunter pet"},gp=true},{q="Why is the Blind Hunter white?",a="The Blind Hunter is an albino bat. Its coloring may have developed in perpetual darkness, far from the sun, unlike bats that venture near the cave mouth.",al={"why is it albino","why is blind hunter white","albino bat"},it="origin"},{q="How does it differ from regular Kraul bats?",a="Common Kraul bats have typical dark coloring and live nearer the entrance, where light still reaches. The Blind Hunter is pale, reclusive, and adapted to the deep tunnels.",al={"kraul bat difference","kraul bat vs blind hunter"}},{q="Whose side is the Blind Hunter on?",a="The Blind Hunter is a wild beast aligned with neither the Razorfen quilboar nor any outside power. It is an apex predator of Razorfen Kraul's pitch-black caverns, surviving purely on animal instinct and treating any trespassers as potential prey.",al={"blind hunter faction","is blind hunter with quilboar","blind hunter side"},it="side",add="7be10a10"},{q="What does the Blind Hunter want?",a="As an untamed subterranean creature, the Blind Hunter harbors no political ambition or malice. It simply hunts to feed and defends its isolated hunting territory in the deepest, lightless caverns of the Kraul from anyone unfortunate enough to stumble into its lair.",al={"blind hunter motive","blind hunter goals","what does the blind hunter want"},it="wants",add="5a3f492c"},{q="Why is the Blind Hunter here?",a="Unlike the common Kraul bats that flutter near the entrance where sunlight filters in, the Blind Hunter makes its home in the deepest, pitch-black reaches of Razorfen Kraul. Having lived in perpetual darkness, it thrives in the hollows far below where it has never seen the light.",al={"why is blind hunter in razorfen","blind hunter location why","blind hunter why here"},it="why_here",add="66c6306f"}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="As a beastmaster crossing the Barrens, you may prize the Blind Hunter as a rare albino beast to tame or as a source of well-crafted subterranean bows."},kw={"albino bat","blind hunter","kraul bat","kraul beast","rare bat","razorfen kraul"},rel={"zone:razorfenkraul","topic:razorfen","topic:light"},src={"Blind Hunter"}}
E["npc:charlga-razorflank"] = {t="npc",n="Charlga Razorflank",z="razorfenkraul",s="In Razorfen Kraul, Charlga Razorflank leads the Razorfen quilboar. They drove the tauren from the southern Barrens, claiming to fight in the name of their fallen god, Agamaggan.",h="In Razorfen Kraul, Charlga Razorflank leads the Razorfen quilboar.",sec={{t="The Crone of the Kraul",b="Charlga Razorflank rules from the tangled brambles of Razorfen Kraul. Her people revere her as a master geomancer, and no quilboar can match her experimental magic. She united her fractious kin into a lethal force. With primal earth and giant thorns growing from the remains of the demigod Agamaggan, Charlga reshaped the Kraul into a fortress that is hard to enter.",sp=0},{t="Expansion and Betrayal",b="Charlga Razorflank sent her warriors against rival tribes and Horde villages across the southern Barrens. Their attacks drove the tauren from their traditional homelands. Charlga also made secret bargains with emissaries of the undead Scourge, trading her unsuspecting tribe's devotion for unnatural power and dark alliances.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Charlga Razorflank?",a="Charlga Razorflank leads the Razorfen quilboar and rules from her lair deep within Razorfen Kraul in the southern Barrens.",al={"charlga lore","who is the crone of the kraul","razorfen boss"},it="identity"},{q="What magic does Charlga use?",a="Charlga Razorflank is a gifted geomancer who commands elemental earth and the great blood-brambles born from the demigod Agamaggan.",al={"charlga abilities","geomancer powers"}},{q="Why did the quilboar attack the tauren in the Barrens?",a="Charlga Razorflank led the Razorfen quilboar against rival tribes and Horde villages, driving the tauren from the southern Barrens.",al={"why do quilboar hate tauren","barrens war quilboar"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Charlga's connection to Razorfen Downs?",a="Razorfen Downs grew from the same mighty vines as Charlga's Kraul. It is the quilboar's traditional capital and home to the Death's Head tribe and its high priests. Charlga rules Razorfen Kraul, not the Downs.",al={"charlga downs","charlga razorfen downs"},it="place"},{q="Why does the Horde want her dead?",a="The tauren and their Horde allies see Charlga as an immediate threat because of her relentless raids, her seizure of their lands, and her dangerous dealings with dark forces.",al={"crone of the kraul quest","why kill charlga"},it="threat"},{q="Whose side is Charlga Razorflank on?",a="Charlga leads the Razorfen quilboar, but she has compromised her people by bargaining with the Scourge. While she claims to champion the quilboar race and the revival of their boar-god Agamaggan, she has secretly allied her tribe with undead ambassadors sent by Amnennar the Coldbringer, serving insidious dark interests beyond her followers' knowledge.",al={"charlga razorflank faction","who does charlga serve","charlga razorflank side"},sp=1,it="side",add="29fd1a6b"},{q="What does Charlga Razorflank want?",a="Charlga seeks absolute dominion over the southern Barrens and total power for her tribe. She drives her people into bloody raids against rival tribes, Horde villages and the tauren, and she has secretly been negotiating with agents of the Scourge, aligning her unsuspecting tribe with the undead for some insidious purpose.",al={"charlga goals","what does charlga want","charlga razorflank motive"},sp=1,it="wants",add="98b63c0f"},{q="Why is Charlga Razorflank here?",a="Razorfen Kraul is the ancestral heart of the Razorfen quilboar, grown from the colossal brambles where Agamaggan fell during the War of the Ancients. As the paramount crone and chieftain of the tribe, Charlga makes her lair at the deepest reaches of the Kraul, where she coordinates her war parties and studies geomantic crystals.",al={"why is charlga in razorfen kraul","charlga razorflank location why","where is charlga"},it="why_here",add="581cf8d6"},{q="Who is Charlga Razorflank tied to?",a="Charlga is tied directly to the Scourge forces infesting Razorfen Downs. She negotiates with emissaries of Amnennar the Coldbringer, the lich who secretly exerts control over the Death's Head quilboar, aligning her unsuspecting tribe with the ranks of the undead.",al={"charlga allies","charlga connections","who is charlga working with"},sp=1,it="ties",add="98250d5e"},{q="Why is Charlga Razorflank famous or feared?",a="Charlga is feared as the Crone of the Kraul, possessing experimental geomantic powers second to none among her kind. Under her iron leadership, the Razorfen quilboar waged savage campaigns that drove the nomadic tauren entirely out of the southern Barrens, earning her a deadly reputation across Kalimdor.",al={"why is charlga feared","how strong is charlga","charlga razorflank power"},it="fame",add="f526ba0c"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Charlga's expansion drove your people from their ancestral lands across the southern Barrens. Defeating her means survival and reclaiming those lands.",["class:Shaman"]="Charlga commands powerful geomantic arts, but her twisting of the elements corrupts sacred primal traditions.",["faction:Horde"]="Defeating Charlga helps secure caravan routes and encampments across the southern Barrens from relentless quilboar war parties."},kw={"agamaggan","barrens","charlga","crone","geomancer","kraul","quilboar","razorflank"},rel={"zone:razorfenkraul","subzone:razorfen-downs-classic","topic:quilboar","topic:agamaggan","topic:scourge","topic:tauren","zone:barrens","quest:1101"},src={"Charlga Razorflank"}}
E["npc:heralath-fallowbrook"] = {t="npc",n="Heralath Fallowbrook",z="razorfenkraul",s="Deep in Razorfen Kraul, Heralath Fallowbrook lies dying in quilboar hands. Sent to investigate the briars around Ancient Agamaggan's remains, he was captured and brutalized. Now he hopes word of his fate and his cherished pendant will reach his wife in Darnassus.",h="Deep in Razorfen Kraul, Heralath Fallowbrook lies dying in quilboar hands.",sec={{t="A Tragic Mission",b="Heralath Fallowbrook came to the southern Barrens to investigate Ancient Agamaggan and the briars spreading around his remains. Sent by his people, the night elf druid sought the source of Razorfen Kraul's corruption. The quilboar captured him instead and locked him in a pen, where beatings and fever left him with mortal wounds. Before he faded, Heralath told Henrig Lonebrow, a dwarf captive, what he had learned. He urged Henrig to warn the sentinel outpost at Thalanaar about the aggression stirred by Charlga Razorflank, the quilboar crone.",sp=0},{t="A Dying Wish",b="Heralath Fallowbrook is too weak to flee Razorfen Kraul, even after Henrig Lonebrow escapes. Near death in the tangled pens, the druid holds on long enough to speak to travelers. He asks them to recover his wife Treshala's pendant from his captors and carry it to her in Darnassus. The pendant will bring Treshala word of his fate, and show that Heralath remembered her to the end.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Heralath Fallowbrook?",a="Heralath Fallowbrook is a night elf druid held captive in Razorfen Kraul. He came to the Barrens to study the corruption of the brambles and the legacy of Ancient Agamaggan, the fallen boar, but the quilboar captured and fatally tortured him.",al={"who is heralath","heralath fallowbrook","night elf in razorfen"},it="identity"},{q="What happened to Heralath inside Razorfen Kraul?",a="The Razorfen quilboar captured Heralath, beat him, and locked him in a hut. Abuse and illness left him near death by the time rescuers could reach him.",al={"why is heralath dying","what happened to heralath fallowbrook"}},{q="What does Heralath ask travelers to do?",a="Heralath asks travelers to recover his wife's pendant from the quilboar and carry it to her in Darnassus, along with word of his fate.",al={"heralath quest","mortality wanes quest"},it="wants"},{q="Who was Henrig Lonebrow to Heralath?",a="Henrig Lonebrow was a dwarf captive held in the same pen as Heralath. Before Henrig escaped, Heralath told him what he knew about Agamaggan and urged him to warn the Thalanaar outpost about Charlga Razorflank's movements.",al={"henrig lonebrow heralath","dwarf captive razorfen"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Heralath Fallowbrook on?",a="Heralath is a night elf loyal to Darnassus and the Alliance. As a druid of his people, he ventured deep into the southern Barrens on their behalf, seeking to understand the strange corruption taking root among the quilboar and to safeguard Kalimdor from whatever darkness stirs within the Kraul.",al={"heralath fallowbrook faction","is heralath alliance","heralath allegiance"},it="side",add="4cf4e465"},{q="Why is Heralath Fallowbrook in Razorfen Kraul?",a="He traveled here to investigate persistent rumors concerning the fallen Ancient Agamaggan and to uncover the root source of the blight corrupting Razorfen Kraul. Unfortunately, his expedition ended in disaster when the ferocious Razorfen quilboar captured him, subjecting him to brutal captivity and fatal wounds.",al={"why is heralath here","heralath purpose in kraul","why did heralath come to razorfen"},it="why_here",add="6e64ea11"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="As a druid, seeing Heralath broken by Razorfen Kraul's brambles shows how unchecked corruption spreads through the southern Barrens.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, carrying Heralath's pendant to Darnassus honors a fallen brother who gave his life trying to understand and heal Kalimdor's wounded lands."},kw={"agamaggan","fallowbrook","henrig lonebrow","heralath","mortality wanes","quilboar","razorfen kraul","treshala"},rel={"quest:1142","npc:treshala-fallowbrook","zone:razorfenkraul","quest:1100","topic:agamaggan","npc:charlga-razorflank","subzone:thalanaar","zone:darnassus"},src={"Heralath Fallowbrook"}}
E["npc:overlord-ramtusk"] = {t="npc",n="Overlord Ramtusk",z="razorfenkraul",s="Deep in Razorfen Kraul, Overlord Ramtusk leads the quilboar warriors into battle. He cries out for victory and for Agamaggan, and his fall breaks the Kraul defenders' martial strength.",h="Deep in Razorfen Kraul, Overlord Ramtusk leads the quilboar warriors into battle.",sec={{t="Warlord of the Kraul",b="Overlord Ramtusk commands the quilboar stronghold deep in Razorfen Kraul, in the southern Barrens. He enters battle with a cry to Agamaggan, the boar demigod, and rules the Kraul's fighters with unyielding authority.",sp=0},{t="Commander of the Kraul",b="Ramtusk directs the quilboar warriors through the Kraul's winding brambles. He keeps tight discipline among the bristled fighters who defend their tribe's sanctum. Elite marksmen flank him as he fights on the front line, bellowing rallying shouts and unleashing slams that can break opposing battle lines in seconds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Overlord Ramtusk?",a="Overlord Ramtusk commands the quilboar warriors deep within Razorfen Kraul. Massive and imposing, he enters battle crying out for victory and for Agamaggan.",al={"who is ramtusk","ramtusk lore","overlord ramtusk"},it="identity"},{q="Where can Overlord Ramtusk be found?",a="Ramtusk commands his elite guards from the thorny heart of Razorfen Kraul, at the southern tip of the Barrens.",al={"ramtusk location","where is ramtusk","overlord ramtusk map"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What enemies has Ramtusk fought in the past?",a="Nothing records Ramtusk's past battles. In the Kraul, he leads his elite guards against any outsider who breaches the briars, crying out for victory and for Agamaggan.",al={"ramtusk enemies","who gave ramtusk scars","ramtusk battle history"},it="history"},{q="What tribe does Ramtusk belong to?",a="Ramtusk belongs to the Razorfen quilboar, who hold Razorfen Kraul in the southern Barrens and revere the boar demigod Agamaggan.",al={"ramtusk faction","ramtusk tribe","what quilboar tribe is ramtusk"},it="people"},{q="Why is Ramtusk targeted by adventurers?",a="Ramtusk leads the Kraul's warriors. His death cripples the quilboar military hierarchy and throws their defensive line into complete disarray.",al={"why kill ramtusk","take them down quest","ramtusk bounty"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How does Ramtusk fight?",a="Ramtusk fights as a battle-hardened warrior. He rallies his cohort with demoralizing cries, staggers enemies with crushing shockwaves, and fights alongside elite ranged bodyguards.",al={"ramtusk tactics","ramtusk combat style","ramtusk abilities"},it="power",gp=true},{q="Whose side is Overlord Ramtusk on?",a="Overlord Ramtusk is a warlord of the quilboar of Razorfen Kraul. He serves the tribe entrenched within the thorny labyrinth, leading their warriors in defense of their ancestral briars and directing their aggression against outsiders encroaching on their territory.",al={"who does ramtusk serve","ramtusk faction","ramtusk loyalty"},it="side",add="26eecf20"},{q="Why is Overlord Ramtusk here in Razorfen Kraul?",a="Ramtusk oversees the defense and martial order of Razorfen Kraul. As overlord of the Kraul's warriors, he directs his troops from deep within the briars, coordinating the tribe's fighters to protect the heart of the kraul against invading enemies.",al={"why is ramtusk here","what is ramtusk doing in razorfen kraul","ramtusk role"},it="why_here",add="a2bf0d01"},{q="Why is Overlord Ramtusk feared?",a="Overlord Ramtusk is a massive quilboar warlord who fights at the head of his elite guards, crying out for victory and for Agamaggan. With crushing blows and rallying war cries, he commands the Kraul's warriors with an authority that strikes dread into any who challenge him.",al={"why is ramtusk feared","how strong is ramtusk","ramtusk reputation"},it="fame",add="b0113e9e"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a Tauren, you know the Barrens' nomadic tribes have fought bitter skirmishes against the Kraul quilboar for generations. Bringing Ramtusk down avenges fallen braves.",["race:Orc"]="As an Orc, you know the quilboar have raided Horde settlements since Durotar and the Barrens outposts were founded. Breaking Ramtusk's command secures the southern Barrens.",["class:Warrior"]="As a Warrior, you see Ramtusk's brutal martial skill in his thunderous strikes and commanding battle shouts, rather than shamanic geomancy or thorn magic."},kw={"barrens","deaths head","overlord ramtusk","quilboar","ramtusk","razorfen kraul"},rel={"zone:razorfenkraul","topic:quilboar","topic:tauren","topic:centaur"},src={"Overlord Ramtusk"}}
E["npc:treshala-fallowbrook"] = {t="npc",n="Treshala Fallowbrook",z="razorfenkraul",s="In Darnassus, Treshala Fallowbrook waits at home for news of her husband. Heralath Fallowbrook has gone far away, into Razorfen Kraul in the Barrens.",h="In Darnassus, Treshala Fallowbrook waits at home for news of her husband.",sec={{t="A Watcher on the Terrace",b="On the second floor of a Tradesmen's Terrace workshop, Treshala Fallowbrook waits for word from her husband. Heralath journeyed to Razorfen Kraul in the Barrens, where thorny growth surrounds the quilboar's warrens. Their marriage is marked by a pendant of bonding, which Heralath carried with him.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Treshala Fallowbrook?",a="Treshala Fallowbrook is on the second floor of a workshop in Darnassus's Tradesmen's Terrace. Climb the wooden ramp inside the weapons building to reach her room.",al={"treshala location","where is fallowbrook","how to find treshala"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What is Treshala researching?",a="Treshala is not a researcher. Her husband, Heralath Fallowbrook, went to Razorfen Kraul, and she waits in Darnassus for news of him and the pendant of bonding he carried there.",al={"treshala quest","mortality wanes lore","what does treshala want"},it="purpose"},{q="Why is she concerned with Razorfen Kraul?",a="Treshala is concerned because her husband, Heralath, ventured into Razorfen Kraul, a thorny quilboar stronghold in the Barrens, and she has had no word of him since.",al={"why razorfen kraul","fallowbrook razorfen","connection to rfk"},it="motive"},{q="Is she a shopkeeper or a craftswoman?",a="Treshala is neither a merchant nor a crafter. She makes her home above the artisan stalls of the Tradesmen's Terrace.",al={"is treshala a vendor","what does she sell"},it="identity"},{q="Who is Treshala Fallowbrook?",a="Treshala Fallowbrook is a night elf living in the Tradesmen's Terrace of Darnassus. Her husband, Heralath Fallowbrook, has journeyed to Razorfen Kraul, and she waits for news of him.",al={"who is treshala","treshala fallowbrook lore","treshala identity"},it="identity",add="145b1f19"},{q="Whose side is Treshala Fallowbrook on?",a="Treshala is aligned with Darnassus and the Alliance. She lives in the night elf capital while her husband, Heralath, is away in Razorfen Kraul.",al={"treshala fallowbrook faction","is treshala alliance","treshala allegiances"},it="side",add="308e08c8"},{q="What does Treshala Fallowbrook want?",a="Treshala's concern is her husband, Heralath Fallowbrook, and the pendant of bonding he carried into Razorfen Kraul. She is the person to whom travelers should bring news of him.",al={"what does treshala want","treshala fallowbrook quest","why does treshala want quillboar items"},it="wants",add="5c8a152e"}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, Treshala's quiet vigil for her husband recalls that since Mount Hyjal, her people no longer have eternity to wait.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion, you may return to Darnassus after expeditions against the quilboar thorn-dens deep in the Barrens. Treshala is there."},kw={"darnassus","fallowbrook","mortality wanes","night elf","razorfen kraul","tradesmen's terrace","treshala"},rel={"quest:1142","subzone:tradesmen-s-terrace","zone:darnassus","zone:razorfenkraul","topic:night-elf","quest:940"},src={"Treshala Fallowbrook"}}
E["quest:1101"] = {t="quest",n="The Crone of the Kraul",z="razorfenkraul",s="At Thalanaar, on the border of Feralas and the Thousand Needles, Falfindel Waywarder sends adventurers after Charlga Razorflank. Henrig Lonebrow's recovered journal reveals the growing danger inside Razorfen Kraul.",h="At Thalanaar, on the border of Feralas and the Thousand Needles, Falfindel Waywarder sends adventurers after...",sec={{t="A Plea at the Border",b="At secluded Thalanaar, the night elf outpost, Falfindel Waywarder grieves for the druid Heralath and the dwarf Henrig Lonebrow. Lonebrow traveled with the Explorers' League before the quilboar captured him. He escaped Razorfen Kraul, but died on the road, leaving a tattered journal that describes the growing menace inside. There is no time to send a runner to Darnassus for military reinforcements. Falfindel sends passing adventurers into the thorned dens to face the danger at its heart.",sp=0},{t="Striking the Chieftain",b="Charlga Razorflank is an ancient geomancer and ruthless matriarch who has united the fractious Razorfen quilboar under her iron rule. From deep within the Kraul, she marshals a bristling army that threatens neighboring lands. Thick thorn mazes, battlement walls, and swarms of fanatical quilboar warriors guard the way to Charlga. Her medallion, taken from her lifeless body, will prove her downfall.",sp=0},{t="A Deeper Corruption",b="Charlga's death blunts the immediate quilboar threat, but leaves the night elves with deeper concerns. The living briars of the Kraul sprouted where the boar Ancient, Agamaggan, fell during the War of the Ancients. When Falfindel receives the medallion, he notes that neutralizing Charlga allows night elf scholars to study the area's corruption more closely. He senses insidious treachery may lie at the root of the sudden blight sweeping Agamaggan's sacred remains.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest The Crone of the Kraul?",a="Falfindel Waywarder, a night elf stationed at Thalanaar, gives it. Thalanaar is an Alliance outpost on the high mountain pass between Feralas and the Thousand Needles.",al={"quest giver crone of the kraul","where do i get crone of the kraul","falfindel waywarder quest"},gp=true},{q="What prerequisite must be completed before starting this quest?",a="First, you must complete Lonebrow's Journal. Retrieve Henrig Lonebrow's journal from his fallen remains near the Great Lift in Thousand Needles, then deliver it to Falfindel in Thalanaar.",al={"prereq for crone of the kraul","how to unlock crone of the kraul","lonebrow journal prerequisite"},gp=true},{q="Who is Charlga Razorflank?",a="Charlga Razorflank is the supreme crone and matriarch of the Razorfen quilboar. A powerful geomancer, she has united the warring tribes within Razorfen Kraul and directs their aggression against neighboring territories.",al={"who is the crone","charlga lore","charlga razorflank"},it="target"},{q="Where can Charlga Razorflank be found?",a="Charlga Razorflank waits at the very end of Razorfen Kraul, in the far southern corner of the Barrens near the Great Lift. She waits atop an altar deep inside the dungeon.",al={"where is charlga","charlga location","where is the crone in rfk"},gp=true},{q="Why does Falfindel need adventurers instead of calling the Darnassus army?",a="Thalanaar is a remote frontier outpost far from northern Kalimdor. Charlga is actively amassing her forces, and word sent to Darnassus would take too long to bring a dispatched army and avert the rising danger.",al={"why not call darnassus","why hire adventurers"},it="why_me"},{q="What proof does Falfindel demand of the crone's death?",a="Falfindel requires Razorflank's Medallion, the amulet Charlga wears, as proof that she has been slain.",al={"what item drops","proof of demise item","razorflank medallion"},it="item"},{q="Why does Falfindel Waywarder want Charlga Razorflank slain?",a="Falfindel Waywarder refuses to let the sacrifices of Heralath and Henrig Lonebrow go in vain. Charlga Razorflank is actively amassing a dangerous force deep within Razorfen Kraul, threatening all surrounding lands. Eliminating her stops this growing quilboar threat and allows the night elves at Thalanaar to safely study how the sacred resting grounds of the Ancient Agamaggan became corrupted.",al={"why kill charlga razorflank","falfindel motive","crone of the kraul why"},it="motive",add="8858b532"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This is the Alliance's main effort against the quilboar menace in the southern Barrens, launched from Thalanaar.",["race:NightElf"]="Night elves grieve over the desecration of Agamaggan's resting place. The boar Ancient fell as an ally of the night elves during the War of the Ancients.",["race:Dwarf"]="Avenging the explorer Henrig Lonebrow gives dwarves a personal stake in storming the quilboar stronghold.",["class:Druid"]="As a druid, you hold Agamaggan in high esteem as a revered Ancient of nature and seek to cleanse the dark taint distorting his thorn-covered legacy."},kw={"agamaggan","charlga razorflank","crone","falfindel waywarder","lonebrow","medallion","razorfen kraul","thalanaar"},rel={"npc:charlga-razorflank","npc:falfindel-waywarder","quest:1100","zone:razorfenkraul","subzone:thalanaar","topic:agamaggan","topic:razorfen","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Falfindel Waywarder",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=1101,ri={"Razorflank's Medallion"}},src={"The Crone of the Kraul"}}
E["quest:1142"] = {t="quest",n="Mortality Wanes",z="razorfenkraul",s="Heralath Fallowbrook lies dying in Razorfen Kraul, with one last plea for the living. He asks that his wife's stolen pendant reach Darnassus, along with word of his death.",h="Heralath Fallowbrook lies dying in Razorfen Kraul, with one last plea for the living.",sec={{t="A Dying Breath in the Thorns",b="In Razorfen Kraul, Heralath Fallowbrook lies mortally wounded among the brambles. The stronghold is overrun by savage quilboar and dark magic, far from Alliance territory. With his strength fading, Heralath manages only broken whispers. He says a brave dwarf named Lonebrow was sent ahead to warn Falfindel. Heralath knows he will not leave the Kraul alive.",sp=0},{t="The Pendant of Bonding",b="Heralath's last wish is to recover the pendant that marks his marriage to Treshala Fallowbrook. One of the lair's aggressors tore it from him. He asks any traveler who stops beside him to carry it across Kalimdor to Darnassus, so Treshala learns of his death instead of waiting in vain.",sp=0},{t="Grief in Darnassus",b="Treshala Fallowbrook receives her husband's recovered pendant in Darnassus and learns that he has died. Devastated, she vows that Heralath's work will not perish with him. She is left to mourn alone and carry his legacy through her sudden grief.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Heralath Fallowbrook?",a="Heralath Fallowbrook is an Alliance night elf found mortally wounded in Razorfen Kraul. As his strength fades, he entrusts passing travelers with recovering his wife's stolen pendant of bonding and taking word of his death to Darnassus.",al={"heralath fallowbrook","who is heralath","dying elf razorfen"},it="identity"},{q="Where is Heralath Fallowbrook located?",a="Heralath Fallowbrook lies inside Razorfen Kraul, the thorn-choked quilboar stronghold in the southern Barrens.",al={"heralath location","where is heralath","where to find heralath"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who was Lonebrow?",a="Lonebrow is a brave dwarf Heralath mentions in his final moments. Heralath says Lonebrow was sent out of the briars to warn Falfindel about the dangers in the Kraul.",al={"dwarf lonebrow","who is lonebrow","lonebrow warning"},it="people"},{q="Who is Treshala Fallowbrook?",a="Treshala Fallowbrook is Heralath's wife and lives in Darnassus. She receives the recovered pendant and learns of her husband's death.",al={"treshala fallowbrook","who is treshala","heralath wife"},it="people"},{q="What is the pendant of bonding?",a="The pendant of bonding is a keepsake that signifies the marriage of Heralath and Treshala Fallowbrook. Quilboar aggressors stole it from Heralath before he died in Razorfen Kraul.",al={"treshalas pendant","what is the pendant","pendant of bonding"},it="item"},{q="How does Treshala react to the news?",a="Treshala is heartbroken and laments the world's cruelty. In her grief, she resolves that Heralath's work must continue through her, then asks to be left alone to mourn.",al={"treshala reaction","what happens when you deliver the pendant"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why does Heralath Fallowbrook want this done?",a="Heralath knows he is dying deep within the hostile thorns of Razorfen Kraul. His final wish in this life is not for his own survival, but to ensure his beloved wife Treshala learns of his fate and receives the cherished pendant of bonding stolen from him by the quilboar before he draws his last breath.",al={"why help heralath","heralath fallowbrook motive","why send the pendant"},it="motive",add="aa8861aa"},{q="Why can't Heralath Fallowbrook retrieve the pendant himself?",a="Heralath is mortally wounded and fading fast, utterly helpless amidst the vicious quilboar of the Kraul. He has barely enough strength left to whisper his final plea, leaving him completely unable to fight his attackers or survive the journey back home to Darnassus on his own.",al={"why does heralath need me","why can't heralath do it","why me mortality wanes"},it="why_me",add="170253dc"}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance champion in the Horde-dominated Barrens, you carry Heralath's final token home to Darnassus as a somber duty of honor.",["race:NightElf"]="As a night elf, you feel the sting of seeing one of your kin perish alone and forgotten in the southern Barrens.",["race:Dwarf"]="As a dwarf, you hear Heralath honor Lonebrow's bravery in carrying an urgent warning away from the quilboar stronghold."},kw={"darnassus","falfindel","heralath fallowbrook","lonebrow","mortality wanes","pendant of bonding","razorfen kraul","treshala fallowbrook"},rel={"npc:heralath-fallowbrook","npc:treshala-fallowbrook","zone:razorfenkraul","zone:darnassus","topic:dwarf"},m={start="Heralath Fallowbrook",["end"]="Treshala Fallowbrook",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1142,ri={"Treshala's Pendant"}},src={"Mortality Wanes"}}
E["quest:1221"] = {t="quest",n="Blueleaf Tubers",z="razorfenkraul",s="Mebok Mizzyrix seeks Blueleaf Tubers beneath the roots of Razorfen Kraul. The Ratchet goblin merchant sends trained snufflenose gophers to find and dig them up for trade.",h="Mebok Mizzyrix seeks Blueleaf Tubers beneath the roots of Razorfen Kraul.",sec={{t="A Prized Subterranean Delicacy",b="Blueleaf tubers are prized as a rare culinary delicacy across the world. They are hard to harvest because they do not grow in open fields or ordinary wild groves. Foragers find them deep underground in the southern Barrens, tangled among the roots of Razorfen Kraul.",sp=0},{t="Mizzyrix's Ingenuity",b="Mebok Mizzyrix, a merchant in Ratchet, devised a way to find the buried tubers. He trains snufflenose gophers, whose noses can catch a tuber's scent from fifty paces away. He supplies foragers with a command stick, a ventilated crate, and an instruction manual to guide the creatures through quilboar territory.",sp=0},{t="Harvesting in the Thorns",b="Harvesting the tubers means entering the lands of the hostile Death's Head quilboar tribe. Foragers must guard their trained gophers from feral beasts and thorny briars in the Kraul, then command the rodents to dig up the buried bulbs. The tubers go back to Ratchet, where Mizzyrix's foreign buyers await.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Blueleaf Tubers used for?",a="Blueleaf Tubers are prized as a rare culinary delicacy around the world. Wealthy buyers pay well for fresh tubers, making them a profitable trade good for goblins like Mebok Mizzyrix.",al={"blueleaf tuber use","what are blueleaf tubers","why collect blueleaf tubers"},it="item"},{q="Where are Blueleaf Tubers found?",a="Blueleaf Tubers lie beneath the earth and thorny roots of the southern Barrens, inside the quilboar stronghold of Razorfen Kraul.",al={"where to find blueleaf tubers","blueleaf tubers location","where do they grow"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do you need a Snufflenose Gopher to find them?",a="The tubers are buried underground and cannot be seen with ordinary eyesight. A snufflenose gopher can smell them from up to fifty paces away and dig them out.",al={"why use gophers","snufflenose gopher purpose","how do gophers find tubers"}},{q="Who is Mebok Mizzyrix?",a="Mebok Mizzyrix is a goblin merchant who works from Ratchet, a neutral port town in the Barrens. He trains native wildlife and acquires exotic goods for foreign trade.",al={"who gives blueleaf tubers quest","mebok mizzyrix lore","ratchet goblin questgiver"},it="identity"},{q="What equipment does Mizzyrix provide for the job?",a="Mizzyrix provides a Crate with Holes containing a trained gopher, a Snufflenose Command Stick to direct its digging, and a Snufflenose Owner's Manual explaining how to handle the beast.",al={"tuber quest items","gopher command stick","crate with holes"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Why can't Mebok gather the tubers himself?",a="Razorfen Kraul is guarded by aggressive quilboar tribes, thorny vines, and dangerous creatures beneath the earth. Mizzyrix sends others into the barrows rather than risk going himself.",al={"why doesnt mebok get them","why hire adventurers"},it="why_me"},{q="Why does Mebok Mizzyrix want Blueleaf Tubers?",a="Mebok Mizzyrix is driven by straightforward goblin commerce: profit. Blueleaf tubers are an exceptionally rare delicacy across the world, found solely deep underground within Razorfen Kraul. Because ordinary foragers cannot easily locate them, they command an extraordinary price. Mebok intends to sell whatever you bring back to his wealthy contacts for a sizable bundle of coin, sharing a modest cut of the proceeds with you for risking life and limb to retrieve them.",al={"mebok mizzyrix motive","why does mebok want tubers","why collect blueleaf tubers"},it="motive",add="8175ef8b"},{q="What is the Crate With Holes for?",a="The Crate With Holes is a specialized transport container built by Mebok to hold a trained snufflenose gopher. The air holes keep the critter alive and breathing comfortably until you reach the depths of Razorfen Kraul, where you can safely release it to begin scenting out buried tubers.",al={"crate with holes use","what is crate with holes","why crate with holes"},it="item",add="e7d11e5c"},{q="What is the Snufflenose Command Stick for?",a="The command stick is a training tool Mebok devised to direct the snufflenose gopher. Wielding it signals the creature to focus its sharp nose, scour the immediate cavern floor, and dig up any hidden blueleaf tubers it scents buried nearby.",al={"command stick purpose","what does snufflenose command stick do","snufflenose command stick"},it="item",add="91901628"},{q="What is the Snufflenose Owner's Manual for?",a="The manual contains Mebok's written instructions outlining how to handle the gopher, direct it with the command stick, and successfully uncover the tubers without losing his trained beast in the quilboar tunnels.",al={"snufflenose manual purpose","what is owners manual for","snufflenose owners manual"},it="item",add="af9e7fb9"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="As a cook, you know blueleaf tubers rank among Azeroth's rarest delicacies. Elite buyers prize their earthy flavor.",["profession:Herbalism"]="As a herbalist, you know blueleaf tubers grow underground among Razorfen's briar roots, away from sunlight.",["faction:Alliance"]="As an Alliance traveler, you can use Mizzyrix's trade contract in neutral Ratchet to enter territory near Horde lands.",["faction:Horde"]="As a Horde warrior defending the Barrens from quilboar incursions, you can earn coin by guiding Mizzyrix's trained gophers through the Kraul."},kw={"blueleaf tubers","command stick","delicacy","mebok mizzyrix","quillboar","ratchet","razorfen kraul","snufflenose gopher","the barrens"},rel={"npc:mebok-mizzyrix","zone:razorfenkraul","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","topic:razorfen","topic:goblin"},m={start="Mebok Mizzyrix",level="26",id=1221,ri={"Blueleaf Tuber","Crate With Holes","Snufflenose Command Stick","Snufflenose Owner's Manual"}},src={"Blueleaf Tubers"}}
E["zone:razorfenkraul"] = {t="dungeon",n="Razorfen Kraul",z="razorfenkraul",s="In the far south of the Barrens, quilboar tribes defend the sacred brambles of Razorfen Kraul. They revere the thickets as the resting place of their ancestor, Agamaggan, while Charlga Razorflank’s rule threatens the region.",h="In the far south of the Barrens, quilboar tribes defend the sacred brambles of Razorfen Kraul.",sec={{t="Blood of the Boar God",b="Ten thousand years ago, during the War of the Ancients, Agamaggan joined the fight against the Burning Legion. The colossal wild god was slain, but his sacrifice preserved life on Azeroth. Legends say massive thorn-covered vines sprang up wherever his blood seeped into the earth, forming thick, defensive labyrinths across the southern plains. The quilboar revere Agamaggan as their divine ancestor and claimed these thickets as holy lands. The greatest became the Razorfen.",sp=0},{t="The Crone's Ambition",b="Charlga Razorflank rules the Razorfen Kraul with despotic force. Under the elder crone’s command, the shamanistic quilboar have left behind their customary territorial skirmishes and now wage coordinated attacks on rival tribes, regional trade routes, and young Horde settlements. Whispers and scout reports tell of undead fiends prowling near the brambles. Charlga may be negotiating with Scourge emissaries, hoping to use forbidden necromancy to strengthen her tribe.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Razorfen Kraul?",a="Razorfen Kraul is a vast network of thorny vines in the southern Barrens. The quilboar hold it as their spiritual heartland and ancestral home.",al={"what is rfk","explain razorfen kraul","razorfen overview"},it="place"},{q="How were the giant thorns created?",a="The enormous brambles sprang from the earth ten thousand years ago, during the War of the Ancients, where the fallen boar demigod Agamaggan’s blood had spilled.",al={"why are there giant thorns","where did the brambles come from","agamaggan thorns"},it="origin"},{q="Who rules Razorfen Kraul?",a="Charlga Razorflank, a ruthless quilboar crone and shaman, rules the Kraul. She commands the Razorfen tribe and directs attacks on neighboring villages and travelers.",al={"who is the boss of rfk","charlga razorflank","crone of the kraul"},it="in_charge"},{q="Why is the Horde concerned about Razorfen Kraul?",a="Quilboar attacks threaten young Horde settlements in the Barrens, and scouts have seen undead near the thickets. Their presence raises fears that Charlga is working with the Scourge.",al={"why does the horde care","horde rfk interest","barrens threat"},it="conflict"},{q="Why are Alliance forces interested in the Kraul?",a="Charlga’s tribe threatens outposts near Feralas and the Thousand Needles. Alliance commanders and scouts at Thalanaar seek her defeat to steady the border.",al={"alliance quests rfk","why alliance go here","thalanaar quest"},it="arrival"},{q="What does defeating Earthcaller Halmgar mean for the story?",a="Earthcaller Halmgar is a rare, influential geomancer deep in the thickets. Defeating him weakens the quilboar’s earth-shaping priesthood, disrupts Charlga Razorflank’s defenses, and hinders their ability to shape Agamaggan’s sacred brambles.",al={"what happens after earthcaller halmgar dies","earthcaller halmgar lore","halmgar defeated"}},{q="Who built all these thorns in Razorfen Kraul?",a="No one built them by hand. Ten thousand years ago during the War of the Ancients, the colossal boar demigod Agamaggan fell fighting the Burning Legion. Where his divine blood soaked into the soil, massive, impenetrable thorn-ridden brambles burst from the earth, forming the labyrinthine thicket you see today.",al={"who made the thorns","who built the thorns","razorfen kraul thorns origin"},it="history",add="59c8bcc4"},{q="What are quilboar?",a="Quilboar are primitive, aggressive boar-like humanoids native to Kalimdor. They have muscular, hunched backs bristling with sharp, defensive quills. Believed to be the mortal offspring of the demigod Agamaggan, they revere his resting places and fiercely defend their thorny territories against any outsiders.",al={"what are quillboar","who are quilboar","quilboar lore"},it="threat",add="4843f165"},{q="Why do the quilboar live in a giant thorn maze?",a="The thorn maze sprouted directly from the blood of their fallen god, Agamaggan. To the quilboar, the Razorfen is sacred ground and his actual resting place. The brambles provide them with both holy reverence and natural, nearly impenetrable fortresses against their regional enemies.",al={"why live in thorns","why do quilboar live here","quilboar thorn maze"},it="motive",add="ea4583b3"},{q="Is Charlga Razorflank the leader of all quilboar?",a="Not of all quilboar, but she rules the powerful Razorfen tribe entrenched within the Kraul. A cunning crone and geomancer, she drove the local tauren from the southern Barrens and commands widespread authority, though rival quilboar tribes scattered across Kalimdor govern themselves independently.",al={"charlga razorflank leader","who leads all quilboar","is charlga in charge of everyone"},it="leader",add="b1fd1d2b"},{q="Who is Agathelos the Raging?",a="Agathelos is a massive, ferocious boar dwelling within Razorfen Kraul. Quilboar revere boars as living symbols of their god Agamaggan, viewing particularly large and tenacious beasts like Agathelos as direct blessings and holy manifestations of the Great Boar's primal power.",al={"who is agathelos","agathelos the raging lore","agathelos giant boar"},it="identity",add="8ed48c28"},{q="Is the Horde poking around Razorfen Kraul too?",a="Yes. Charlga Razorflank's raiders continually stage brutal assaults on Horde settlements throughout the Barrens and drove the tauren from their ancestral southern ranges. Both the orcs and tauren are actively dispatching warriors to break the crone's power and end the quilboar threat.",al={"is the horde here","horde presence razorfen","horde in razorfen kraul"},it="conflict",add="4f663063"},{q="Who is Agamaggan?",a="Agamaggan the Great Boar was an Ancient Guardian and one of the first, most powerful Wild Gods to walk Azeroth. Revering him as their creator, the quilboar worship his memory, drawing spiritual and geomantic power from his blood and the vast thorn clusters born of his sacrifice.",al={"who is agamaggan","agamaggan the great boar","agamaggan lore"},it="history",add="5328604f"},{q="Did Agamaggan die in the War of the Ancients?",a="Yes. Ten thousand years ago, Agamaggan answered Cenarius's call to defend Azeroth from the Burning Legion. He rampaged across the continent, crushing thousands of demons before finally falling in battle against overwhelming demonic legions, sacrificing his life so Malfurion Stormrage could reach the Well of Eternity.",al={"how did agamaggan die","agamaggan war of the ancients","did agamaggan die"},it="history",add="bc4e6730"},{q="Do the quilboar worship Agamaggan still?",a="They do, with fanatical devotion. Quilboar shamans and geomancers pray to Agamaggan for strength in battle, venerate giant boars as his blessings, and hoard Blood Shards formed from his petrified blood. They believe his physical remains protect them and their sacred home.",al={"do quilboar still worship agamaggan","quilboar religion","worship of agamaggan"},it="motive",add="e47b7687"},{q="What are the Death's Head guys?",a="The Death's Head is a militant quilboar faction led on the battlefield by Overlord Ramtusk, operating alongside the Razorfen tribe. Ramtusk directs their disciplined, battle-hardened troops to maintain a stranglehold on the thorn maze and wage vicious wars against their neighbors.",al={"deaths head tribe","who are the deaths head","deaths head quilboar"},it="identity",add="7583b13a"},{q="Are the quilboar here going to attack Barrens settlements?",a="They already are. Under Crone Charlga Razorflank's command, aggressive raiding parties constantly sweep out from the thorns into the surrounding lands. They have harassed travelers near the Great Lift, assaulted rival tribes, and pushed Horde settlements and caravans to the brink of open war.",al={"will quilboar attack barrens","barrens under attack quilboar","quilboar raids barrens"},it="threat",add="4bc36485"},{q="What is the difference between the Kraul and the Downs?",a="Both are massive thorn networks spawned by Agamaggan's fall, but they serve different roles. Razorfen Kraul is the ancestral heart where Charlga Razorflank marshals living quilboar raiders. Razorfen Downs, located further southeast near the demigod's massive skeletal maw, has fallen under the darker influence of the Scourge.",al={"difference between kraul and downs","razorfen kraul vs downs","kraul or downs"},it="place",add="ed4c33ec"},{q="Is the Scourge involved in Razorfen?",a="Yes. Disturbing reports and captured missives reveal that Charlga Razorflank has begun negotiating with agents of the Scourge. Scouts have sighted undead encroaching near the Razorfen, raising dire concerns that the Lich King's minions seek a foothold on Kalimdor through these unsuspecting tribes.",al={"scourge in razorfen","are undead in razorfen","scourge presence kraul"},sp=1,it="threat",add="974f5634"},{q="Who is Amnennar?",a="Amnennar the Coldbringer is a powerful agent of the Scourge who has established himself in the neighboring Razorfen Downs. Working behind the scenes, he manipulates the quilboar leadership and commands the Death's Head forces to transform the southern brambles into an undead stronghold.",al={"who is amnennar","amnennar the coldbringer","amnennar lore"},sp=1,it="identity",add="a384c7af"},{q="How did I end up in Razorfen Kraul?",a="You traveled to the southernmost reaches of the Barrens, near the towering bluffs overlooking Thousand Needles. Pushing through the contested scrublands, you found the immense thicket of blood-nourished briars that sprang from the corpse of the ancient boar god Agamaggan. Carved directly into these massive, petrified thorn vines lies the western entrance to the Kraul, where quilboar defenders guard the approach against any who dare encroach on their sacred territory.",al={"how did i get here","how do you reach razorfen kraul","where is razorfen kraul"},it="arrival",add="af015f4e"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Razorfen Kraul?",a="You are here to break the hostile power of the Razorfen tribe and halt their aggressive expansion across the Barrens. Under the guidance of their crone, Charlga Razorflank, these fanatic quilboar have stepped up violent assaults on neighboring settlements and caravans. Your goal is to fight through the winding thorn passages, shatter the Death's Head leadership, and cut down Charlga before her dark geomancy and suspected dealings with sinister undead forces ignite an all-out war.",al={"what is my mission here","why am i in razorfen kraul","what am i doing here"},it="purpose",add="141f6ea5"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="As a tauren, you know the quilboar have long contested Mulgore’s borders. Their dark alliances and harm to the earth make the Kraul a matter of tribal defense.",["class:Shaman"]="As a shaman, you see how quilboar geomancy twists the earth and elements around Agamaggan’s blood, turning primal powers to savage ends.",["faction:Horde"]="As a member of the Horde, you help protect supply wagons and young settlements across the southern Barrens by curbing the Kraul’s aggression.",["race:Undead"]="As an undead, you may take interest in the strange reagents, bat guano, and reports of Scourge incursions among the briars."},kw={"agamaggan","barrens","charlga","halmgar","kraul","quilboar","ramtusk","razorfen","razorflank","scourge"},rel={"topic:agamaggan","topic:quilboar","topic:razorfen","npc:charlga-razorflank","npc:overlord-ramtusk","quest:1101","subzone:great-lift","subzone:thalanaar"},m={levels="29-38"},src={"Razorfen Kraul (Classic)","Razorfen Kraul"}}
